#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
mkdebinitrd - build a Debian initramfs from scratch that boots with busybox init.

The image is a complete (minbase-style) Debian userland: dpkg and apt work, so
packages can be installed at runtime with apt-get.  Busybox provides PID 1
(/init -> busybox init), early mounts, module coldplug and DHCP networking.

No Debian tooling is needed on the build host: the Release/Packages indices are
fetched and verified here, dependencies are resolved here, and .deb files are
unpacked with the host's GNU tar.  Package configuration (maintainer scripts)
runs in a chroot when the host can execute target binaries (same arch, or a
qemu-user binfmt handler).  When it cannot, packages are registered as
"unpacked" and configured by busybox init on boot.

Requires: Linux, root, python3 >= 3.6, GNU tar, cpio, and the chosen compressor.
"""

